1. Code copied from omp (https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi, MIT License)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These files hold text or logic taken from omp's source, as of omp 18.18.3. They carry omp's copyright and license, which
are reproduced below. `bank_id.ts` and `omp_redact.ts` also say so in their own headers; the other files below do not, so
this list is where their origin is recorded.

- vendor/memory_import/omp_redact.ts: a copy of `redactMemorySecrets` and the helpers it needs, from omp's coding agent
  (packages/coding-agent/src/memory-backend/redact.ts). The importer applies the same redaction omp applies to every
  memory write. It is copied because that file ships in the coding agent, not in the npm package the importer uses.
- vendor/memory_import/bank_id.ts: a copy of `projectBankSegment` (packages/coding-agent/src/mnemopi/config.ts), the
  function that gives a project folder its bank name, for the same reason. `omp-memory doctor` checks it against your banks.
- vendor/omp_hub/test_memory_schema.py: the table, index and trigger definitions of omp's Mnemopi library
  (packages/mnemopi), as they appear in a bank the library created. Tests use them to build scratch banks.
- vendor/memory_import/lib.ts (`PARITY_REQUIREMENTS`): a few SQL statements quoted from the Mnemopi library's source. They are
  search strings: before any write, the importer looks for them in the installed library and in the omp binary.
- vendor/memory_import/test/redact.test.ts and test/bank-id.test.ts: the expected values were produced by running those
  two omp functions on fixed inputs.

The rest of the code in this repository (the command line, the importer, the backup scripts, the tests) is original work
under this repository's license. The code under vendor/ is copied byte for byte from a separate source tree (see
docs/vendoring.md); that does not change who wrote it.

