2. Packages that `omp-memory setup` downloads (not part of this repository)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing below is copied into this repository or redistributed by it. `omp-memory setup` is a command you run yourself; it
prints what it will fetch, then downloads these from the npm registry (https://registry.npmjs.org) into
`~/.cache/omp-memory/lib/<omp version>/`, and the embedding runtime and model from the hosts named below into omp's own
cache (`~/.omp/cache/fastembed*`). Each package keeps its own license, which is in the package. No other command of
omp-memory downloads anything, except `import --apply` when `setup` was skipped and it has to fetch the embedding
runtime or model itself.

The Mnemopi library, installed with `bun add --exact @oh-my-pi/pi-mnemopi@<the version omp --version prints>`. Every package
below is at that same version (checked for 18.18.3 on 2026-11-11), and all are MIT licensed:

    @oh-my-pi/pi-mnemopi            MIT   the library the importer writes banks through
    @oh-my-pi/pi-ai                 MIT
    @oh-my-pi/pi-catalog            MIT
    @oh-my-pi/pi-natives            MIT
    @oh-my-pi/pi-natives-<os>-<cpu> MIT   one package for your platform (for example darwin-arm64, linux-arm64); it
                                          carries a THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt for the native code it contains
    @oh-my-pi/pi-utils              MIT
    @oh-my-pi/pi-wire               MIT
    @oh-my-pi/omptype               MIT

